  body: |
    # Industrial Injuries international residence and presence scope

    ## Authored interpretation

    The guidance covers named Industrial Injuries benefits and distinguishes domestic conditions, EC provisions and reciprocal agreements when considering residence and presence.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 074360–074362 list Disablement Benefit, Reduced Earnings Allowance, Retirement Allowance and Industrial Death Benefit. The chapter directs other schemes elsewhere. No extension to ESA or to every industrial-injury payment is inferred.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 074360, PDF page 91](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/692421b6367485ea116a55db/dmg-ch-07-part-04.pdf#page=91)
    - [DMG 074362, PDF page 91](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/692421b6367485ea116a55db/dmg-ch-07-part-04.pdf#page=91)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

