    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part4/0091
      quote: "074361 The guidance covers\n\n\n• claims to benefit, including UK law (074370 - 074378) and European Community law (074379 -\n074392) and reciprocal agreements and claims from outside Great Britain (074430 - 074431) and\n\n\n• export of benefit to other countries, including Great Britain law (074440 - 074449) and European\nCommunity law (074450 - 074454) and reciprocal agreements (074460)."
      locator: DMG 074361
  - target: term/intl-reciprocal-benefit-scope
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The Industrial Injuries passage identifies reciprocal agreements as a distinct possible source after domestic and EC conditions; agreement and benefit coverage remain to be checked.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part4/0091
      quote: "074362 If a claimant does not satisfy the conditions in Great Britain law, the decision maker should\nconsider whether the claimant is helped by European Community law and, if not, by any reciprocal\nagreements."
      locator: DMG 074362
    - page: page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part1/0057
      quote: "070310 The UK has reciprocal agreements with both EEA countries and other countries. Lists of the\ncountries with which the UK has agreements are at\n\n\n• DMG 070330 for EEA countries and\n\n\n• DMG 070333 for non-EEA countries.\n\n\nThose lists also set out which benefits are covered by the agreements."
      locator: DMG 070310
